  "definition": "epoch 0 = the schedule T0 coincides with the first held FNAF2_NIGHT frame on the helper image clock (@fnaf2-1020/adapters/night-onset, NIGHT_ONSET_HOLD_MS 500); positive epoch fires the schedule later (minus-toys-plan: when = base + at + epochMs); the executor delivers T0 = onset + aimMs + k*periodMs. The period is 5000 ms because the band is set by Withered Foxy's roll timer (g337, Every 5000 ms: 21 + Random(5) - D <= AI) against the route's 10 s cycle; a one-second scan (death-prediction phases 0..950) never sees it.",
  "why": "Night 6 with the hallfix knobs (fnv1a-44e8eff2) scores 0/3000 at every epoch in [0, 1000) and dies to Foxy on the phone (26 s, 238 s). The same knobs score 3000/3000 across effective epochs 2900-4950: there the 5 s roll ticks fall at cycle phases where D (reset by the camdrop at phase 3.65 and the flash at 10.06, doubled while masked 4.25-9.46) is below 21 + Random(5) - AI. The band is perforated every 200 ms by 50 ms holes where the split-camera arming fails (g263 samples last viewed on a 200 ms timer; the CAM 09 tap and the monitor drop 50 ms apart straddle a tick, the raise restores CAM 09, the box is never wound and the Puppet kills at ~36-50 s). The aim 3600 puts the effective interval [3800, 3885] inside the window [3766.67, 3916.67) with 33 ms to each hole. The latency is the measured monitor-up press-to-effect median 253 ms (2026-09-12) with stated bounds; the arming CAM taps themselves are unmeasured.",
